            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0656" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2598a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-27T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9441. French apparently unwilling to proceed with $25,000,000 four power loan to
                    China unless disbandment of certain troops appears as condition precedent.
                    England has agreed with us and we are just advised Japan agrees with England.
                    Please cable why French Government takes this attitude. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
